  "feedback": "The Mohr→hypercube conceptual link is genuinely strong — Mohr literally pioneered 4D cube art, so 'bloom-burst' as organic flowering of his geometry is a smart swerve. The quantized positions (PS=0.35 grid snap) honor the pixel/computational lineage well. Two things to refine: the fill-dust particles (random scatter in the 28×28×24 box) dilute the tesseract's clean silhouette — cut them to ≤15% of budget or confine them to a tight halo around the edges so the hypercube reads instantly. Second, the bloom petals (fibonacci-sphere burst at each vertex) risk reading as uniform fuzzballs at 180 petals per vertex; elongate them along the adjacent edge directions so each bloom has directional 'sepals' that echo the cube geometry rather than generic spheres."
